        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>AFAR: An Interactive Horror Film</strong> is a DIY survival horror experience where you control the story. Inspired by classic 90s FMV adventures, survival horror games, and the grainy unease of VHS nightmares, AFAR blends film and gameplay into one unsettling journey.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as <strong>Brian Everette</strong>, a paranormal investigator searching for the missing contestants of the hit reality show <i>AFAR</i>. What begins as a simple missing persons case unravels into a chilling descent through shifting paths, haunted rainforests, and choices that will test your nerve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Shot and created entirely by one person deep in the rainforests of Australia, AFAR embodies true independent spirit—handmade, unpredictable, and filled with atmosphere. Every decision you make pulls you further into the nightmare, and no two playthroughs are exactly the same.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Interactive Horror Film</strong> – Choose your path and shape the narrative through branching decisions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>DIY Terror</strong> – Built entirely solo, blending gritty filmmaking with survival horror gameplay.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Classic Inspirations</strong> – A love letter to 90s FMV games, survival horror, and analog VHS chills.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Replayable Paths</strong> – Multiple routes and outcomes encourage players to dive back in.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Five Distinct Endings</strong> – Your decisions lead to one of five possible fates—will you uncover the truth, or be lost to the nightmare forever?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Atmosphere</strong> – Shot in real locations across the Australian rainforest, giving the film a raw, haunting authenticity.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Do you dare to step into the unknown—and see how far <i>AFAR</i> goes?</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>AFAR: An Interactive Horror Film</strong> is a DIY survival horror experience where you control the story. Inspired by classic 90s FMV adventures, survival horror games, and the grainy unease of VHS nightmares, AFAR blends film and gameplay into one unsettling journey.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as <strong>Brian Everette</strong>, a paranormal investigator searching for the missing contestants of the hit reality show <i>AFAR</i>. What begins as a simple missing persons case unravels into a chilling descent through shifting paths, haunted rainforests, and choices that will test your nerve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Shot and created entirely by one person deep in the rainforests of Australia, AFAR embodies true independent spirit—handmade, unpredictable, and filled with atmosphere. Every decision you make pulls you further into the nightmare, and no two playthroughs are exactly the same.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Interactive Horror Film</strong> – Choose your path and shape the narrative through branching decisions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>DIY Terror</strong> – Built entirely solo, blending gritty filmmaking with survival horror gameplay.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Classic Inspirations</strong> – A love letter to 90s FMV games, survival horror, and analog VHS chills.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Replayable Paths</strong> – Multiple routes and outcomes encourage players to dive back in.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Five Distinct Endings</strong> – Your decisions lead to one of five possible fates—will you uncover the truth, or be lost to the nightmare forever?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Atmosphere</strong> – Shot in real locations across the Australian rainforest, giving the film a raw, haunting authenticity.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Do you dare to step into the unknown—and see how far <i>AFAR</i> goes?</p>",
